    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (81.41), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against Luinder Avila and JP Sears, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** is the clear anchor of the day; he draws significant value from a strong platoon advantage against the right-handed Avila, and his spot in the three-hole, coupled with the favorable park factors, maximizes his potential for runs and RBI. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** capitalizes on a dynamic platoon edge against the left-handed Sears, providing a massive boost to his base projection. In the outfield, **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Andy Pages** (74.02) are primed for production; **Andy Pages** specifically benefits from the slow delivery of Eduardo Rodriguez, which increases his probability of swiping a bag, a crucial consideration given the scarcity of stolen bases in our current 5x5 build.\n\nThe toughest bench decision of the morning involves **Heliot Ramos**, who narrowly missed the cut with a score of 54.25. While **Heliot Ramos** benefits from hitting leadoff and carries additional upside from favorable wind conditions, the optimizer prioritized the higher floor and platoon-advantaged profiles of our middle-of-the-order hitters. Our starters are generally well-positioned, though we must remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all rostered hitters; should **Drake Baldwin** or **Coby Mayo** be shifted lower in their respective batting orders upon the official release, their current scoring efficiency could drop. **Josh Lowe** (67.37) remains a high-interest play due to his 100% stolen base expectation against the Zebby Matthews delivery, providing a rare opportunity to bank speed in a category where we cannot afford to fall behind. We will continue to monitor weather patterns and confirmed lineups to ensure our daily caps are deployed with maximum efficiency.",
